  "goodToKnow": "Die Grammatik is grammar, and also a grammar book. Mark Twain's essay The Awful German Language (1880) famously mocked German Grammatik: der, die, das, four cases and verbs at the end. Learners take comfort that German grammar is very regular once you know the rules. The Duden publishes the standard Grammatik. Grammatisch richtig means grammatically correct. Stress: gra-MA-tik."
